# Deep-Guard Fix — 2026-07-10T20:07:15+03:30
# File: /tmp/dvna/core/appHandler.js  Line: 10  Severity: critical
# Type: auth_issue

## Root Cause
The current code constructs an SQL query by directly concatenating user input, making it susceptible to SQL injection.

## Explanation
The proposed patch uses parameterized queries to safely include user input in the SQL query, preventing attackers from injecting malicious SQL code. By using Sequelize's query method with bind parameters, the input is properly escaped and treated as data rather than part of the SQL command.

## Patch
--- a/tmp/dvna/core/appHandler.js
+++ b/tmp/dvna/core/appHandler.js
@@ -10,6 +10,6 @@
  var query = "SELECT name,id FROM Users WHERE login='" + req.body.login + "'";
- db.sequelize.query(query, {
+ db.sequelize.query("SELECT name,id FROM Users WHERE login = :login", {
      model: db.User,
+     replacements: { login: req.body.login }
   }).then(user => {

